From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: buildroot-lab <buildroot-lab@localhost>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bootstrap link failure from GHS Multi generator header

cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h was included unconditionally on Linux,
even during CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP builds where cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.cxx
is never compiled (the bootstrap script's hardcoded source list only
adds GHS/MinGW sources for the MinGW case). The header's inline
NewFactory() method still references the out-of-line constructor,
so any host toolchain that doesn't eliminate the unused inline
function emits an unresolved weak symbol, causing:

  undefined reference to `cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator::cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator(cmake*)'

during the final `cmake` bootstrap link. Guard the include with
!defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP) to match the guard already used around the
generator's registration in AddDefaultGenerators().

Signed-off-by: buildroot-lab <buildroot-lab@localhost>
---
 Source/cmake.cxx | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/cmake.cxx b/Source/cmake.cxx
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/Source/cmake.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmake.cxx
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 #  include "cmExtraEclipseCDT4Generator.h"
 #endif

-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(_WIN32)
+#if !defined(CMAKE_BOOTSTRAP) && (defined(__linux__) || defined(_WIN32))
 #  include "cmGlobalGhsMultiGenerator.h"
 #endif

--
